--TEST--
`[log] target` is one destination and both of `rule:errors/record-producers`'s writers land in it, so a deployment that names a file collects the program's records and the engine floor's in the same place and neither keeps a channel of its own beside it — `rule:errors/engine-floor` and `rule:errors/record-producers`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:errors/record-producers`'s sameness, one step past the record's shape: the two writers
// agree about the *destination* as well as about the envelope. With
// `[log] target` naming a file, `Core\Log::write` no longer writes the
// program's own output and the floor no longer writes the diagnostic channel —
// both land in the operator's file, which is what makes a named target one
// destination rather than two copies of the configuration.
//
// The floor is reached without ending the run: a `Core\Script::onExit` hook
// that throws is reported through `nvs_runtime::floor::report` and abandoned,
// and the drain continues to the next hook (`rule:observability/a-hook-observes-and-never-steers`). That is the one
// place a floor record is written with user code still to run, so it is the
// only place the file can be read back from inside the program that filled it.
Core\Script::onExit(fn (): void => {
    throw new RuntimeError("the floor said so");
});

// FIFO, so this runs after the hook above has already been reported.
Core\Script::onExit(fn (): void => {
    echo Core\IO::readText("app.log");
});

Core\Log::write(Core\Log\Level::Error, "the application said so");

// Printed *before* either record, which is the displacement asserted from the
// outside: with no target configured this line would come second, after
// `Core\Log::write` had written the same stream.
echo "the program's own output\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[log]
target = "file:app.log"

[capabilities.fs]
read = ["."]
--EXPECTF--
the program's own output
{"level":"error","msg":"the application said so","source":{"file":"case.nvs","line":23}}
{"level":"error","msg":"the floor said so","fields":{"class":"RuntimeError","origin":"exit-hook"},"nodes":%s}
